{%- doc -%}
  Outline icon for an engagement ring setting, drawn as the stones themselves, to read at ~28px
  beside a menu link. Companion to 'icon-diamond-shape', which draws the cut of a single stone;
  these draw how the stones of a setting are arranged.

  There is no band on any of them: what tells these styles apart is the stones, and a band drawn
  at this size only crowds them. Every round stone is the same brilliant - girdle, crown break,
  table, and the facets between - so a column of them reads as one set.

  @param {string} style - one of solitaire, side-stone, halo, hidden-halo, three-stone,
    bridal-sets, vintage, nature-inspired, toi-et-moi, promise
{%- enddoc -%}

<svg
  class="icon-ring-style"
  viewBox="0 0 24 24"
  fill="none"
  stroke="currentColor"
  stroke-width="0.9"
  stroke-linejoin="round"
  stroke-linecap="round"
  aria-hidden="true"
  focusable="false"
>
  {%- case style -%}
        {%- comment -%}
      One stone and nothing else, drawn nearly the full box: the girdle, the eight upper girdle
      facets, the star, and the table. The one icon in the set with the whole crown drawn - at the
      size the others are set, that much facet work closes up.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- when 'solitaire' -%}
      <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10.4"/>
      <ellipse cx="12" cy="4.2" rx="2" ry="2.5"/>
      <ellipse cx="12" cy="4.2" rx="2" ry="2.5" transform="rotate(45 12 12)"/>
